ct examples, without requiring eight rows or specified status and area counts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen if SeedData.Run is invoked more than once while demo seeding is enabled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Do not insert duplicate demo rows on repeated runs.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"For create-request validation, should the API implement only the validation and error details defined by the locked OpenAPI contract, or also enforce the product document’s explicit field limits and messages wherever they differ or are absent from the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use only the validation and errors defined by the locked OpenAPI contract.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"If PostgreSQL is unreachable, should the application fail during startup, or start successfully and fail only when an operation needs the database?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup when PostgreSQL cannot be reached; do not fall back to another store.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the existing GET / health endpoint remain alongside the four contract operations, or should it be removed so the API exposes only the operations in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the existing GET / health endpoint in addition to the four contract operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Make the Maintenance Requests API list requests by descending creation time, validate status filters, and return the specified errors for list failures.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Implement request creation with trimmed fields, system-assigned IDs and timestamps, Open status, optional descriptions, contract validation, and the specified error responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement retrieval by request ID and status updates, allowing only Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open, with the specified success and error responses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Persist requests in the configured PostgreSQL database, ensure the request schema is available at startup, and preserve records across restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Seed at least three specified contract-example requests with positive system-assigned IDs and UTC timestamps; ensure repeated seeding leaves exactly one row per selected title.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Run demo seeding at startup only when Seed:Demo is true, and do not add demo rows when it is false or unset.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Fail startup if PostgreSQL is unavailable, without switching to another data store.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Keep GET / returning HTTP 200 with the response body \\\"API is up\\\".\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Do not provide maintenance-request screens or web-app screen-flow tests in the API repository.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}